{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/766038-rules-question-chain-of-command-b-s","id":766038,"title":"Rules Question: Chain of Command (B&S)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-14T21:10:22-08:00","id":766038,"title":"Rules Question: Chain of Command (B&S)","content":"Chain of Command states that you can implant one of your Dominate effects within someone, but since every Dominate effect requires the victim to first be Mesmerised, does that mean you have to spend 4 vitae and roll twice to implant both a Mesmerise command and whichever power you actually want to use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T12:24:35-08:00","id":766458,"title":"","content":"No, you just spend 2 Vitae and roll Presence + Presuasion + Dominate vs. the victim's Resolve + Blood Potency. If you win the contested roll or the victim relents, you state what Dominate power you want them to use and who you want them to use it on. Then when the victim sees that person, they roll to activate that power, using what ever dice pool you would use if you were to activate that power yourself. No additional Vitae cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T17:34:57-08:00","id":766679,"title":"","content":"Then there's really no point in implanting any power except Mesmerise because Iron Edict, Entombed Command, The Lying Mind and Possession will all automatically fail if the target isn't Mesmerised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T03:53:43-08:00","id":766973,"title":"","content":"Correct. You can't use Chain of Command to implant more than one power usage in an individual at a time. But since it counts as &quot;you&quot; mesmerizing the person, you <u>could</u> use someone else (like a coterie member) to install the mesmerized condition on another target then approach them later that night and use one of the other powers straight out. If you have a ghoul whom you've taught the first rank of Dominate, you have them mesmerize the person under their own power, then insert another power (like Possession) which they can use employing your dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T06:10:38-08:00","id":768449,"title":"","content":"OUCH Never thought of this...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T05:21:14-08:00","id":769879,"title":"","content":"Can\u00b4t you setup a sequence of chains of command with more than one host, send in person one with Mesmerize, person 2 with Iron Edcit and so on and so forth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:34:38-08:00","id":769929,"title":"","content":"Yes but keep in mind the activation costs. It's a good way to get around/exploit regulations in a domain where one is responsible for the actions of their minions. Get your enemies' minions to do it for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":".  I'm a punctuation fascist 11-20-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T16:38:32-08:00","id":770373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/766038-rules-question-chain-of-command-b-s?p=769879#post769879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can\u00b4t you setup a sequence of chains of command with more than one host, send in person one with Mesmerize, person 2 with Iron Edcit and so on and so forth?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think about that, thanks. I'll bring it up with my ST but I think they will probably rule that since Person 1 Mesmerised the target Person 1 has to be the one to use further powers on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T17:01:53-08:00","id":770382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/766038-rules-question-chain-of-command-b-s?p=770373#post770373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't think about that, thanks. I'll bring it up with my ST but I think they will probably rule that since Person 1 Mesmerised the target Person 1 has to be the one to use further powers on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could argue that the person is just a vector to your power, its not them Mesmerizing, it you through them, its even rolled with your own dice pool not the host's. If he rules that the host is mesmerizing then you will have to discard tsusai's suggestion also (that you can send a host mesmerizer to then hit with Iron Edict).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T19:05:46-08:00","id":770449,"title":"","content":"Of course, the downside of that being the case is I can''t give a ghoul or childe with much lower levels of Dominate a higher use power they can activate after they Mesmerise the target themselves. Neither would I be able to give them a higher dice pool Mesmerise so they can then use Iron Edict which requires no rolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T19:28:28-08:00","id":770462,"title":"","content":"Yah, each approach has its downsides. I'm a bit lazy now to think about what is more consistent with the intention behind the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T03:46:43-08:00","id":770632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/766038-rules-question-chain-of-command-b-s?p=770373#post770373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't think about that, thanks. I'll bring it up with my ST but I think they will probably rule that since Person 1 Mesmerised the target Person 1 has to be the one to use further powers on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The person/people installing the various dominate commands all derive their power to do so from the same individual, it says so in the description. If your ST rules that, then don't buy the power or get your XP back that you spent on it because it's obvious that the ST doesn't want you using other people to install your dominate commands which is the actual purpose of the devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 11-21-2015, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T05:54:19-08:00","id":777702,"title":"","content":"Did rules for &quot;stacking&quot; be fixed in errata? Because:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To target the heart, make an attack roll with a \u20133 die penalty after factoring Defense. If the attack causes <b>five points</b> of damage, it penetrates the heart. </div> </div> </div> which means, you need roll at very least 4 successes (+1 for stake, I guess)/<br /> Am I only one who think, that it is too much. While supernaturals can do this (in theory), mortals have literally no chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T06:36:54-08:00","id":777716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/766038-rules-question-chain-of-command-b-s?p=777702#post777702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did rules for &quot;stacking&quot; be fixed in errata? Because:<br /> which means, you need roll at very least 4 successes (+1 for stake, I guess)/<br /> Am I only one who think, that it is too much. While supernaturals can do this (in theory), mortals have literally no chance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well in my opinion the rule is ok. for a mortal, stake the someone's heart while he is conscious is quite a pure miracle. I means, someone that can apply his defense...is enough for him to shift his position of just two cm to avoid the impalament.<br /> Different is while the target is unconscious or is taken with a surprise attack. In that case it becomes possible even for mortal.<br /> <br /> Probably I lost something. Why this question in this topic? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T06:41:21-08:00","id":777719,"title":"","content":"Hard, almost imposible to do by an average person in the middle of a fight? Yes, working as intended. A lot easier to do to an sleeping vampire, specially with the help of a hammer.<br /> <br /> EDIT: now that Marcus mentioned it... yeah, what is this question doing here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}